{"uid":"3a26a8d18b813ab6","name":"test_a_configured_run_wide_ceiling_stops_a_repeated_reject_then_cure_cycle_at_a_terminal_state","fullName":"tests.test_cure_pass#test_a_configured_run_wide_ceiling_stops_a_repeated_reject_then_cure_cycle_at_a_terminal_state","historyId":"c68970beb639cd4644d324e451b92c57","time":{"start":1791925594500,"stop":1791925594575,"duration":75},"description":"Task 002 (PRD requirement A.2, #192): the cure pass is bounded and\n    declared -- `JobConfig.cure_pass_ceiling` (job.yaml key\n    `cure_pass_ceiling`, default 3, stated in `docs/api.md`'s `curePasses`/\n    `gateCurePasses` rows) caps how many cure passes ONE RUN may take, and\n    both rejection sites read that ceiling from configuration\n    (`self.cfg.cure_pass_ceiling`) instead of the module-level\n    `CURE_PASS_CEILING` literal they read before this task.\n\n    The quantity bounded is the RUN-wide total across every approach and\n    both cure channels (`LoopSupervisor._cure_passes_for_run`: review's\n    `curePasses` plus the gate's `gateCurePasses`), which is what makes the\n    requirement's claim -- \"a run cannot loop cure -> reject -> cure\n    indefinitely\" -- actually true. A per-approach cap cannot: every replan\n    starts an approach whose own counter reads `0`, so the cycle would run\n    on for as many approaches as the run has budget for.\n\n    Configured to **2** here, below the module default of 3, and driven as a\n    repeated reject-then-cure sequence: review spends pass 1, the peer gate\n    spends pass 2 out of the SAME run budget, and every rejection after\n    that -- including the FIRST rejection over a freshly replanned approach,\n    which a per-approach cap would have granted -- is refused by the ceiling\n    alone, with all blocking findings still `curable: true` throughout (no\n    incurable finding, no criteria-tamper finding, no superset repeat is\n    doing the stopping). The refusals fall through to the ordinary\n    replan-then-finish edges and the run reaches `failed`, a\n    `state.TERMINAL_STATES` member, instead of curing forever.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 002 (PRD requirement A.2, #192): the cure pass is bounded and<br />\ndeclared -- <code>JobConfig.cure_pass_ceiling</code> (job.yaml key<br />\n<code>cure_pass_ceiling</code>, default 3, stated in <code>docs/api.md</code>'s <code>curePasses</code>/<br />\n<code>gateCurePasses</code> rows) caps how many cure passes ONE RUN may take, and<br />\nboth rejection sites read that ceiling from configuration<br />\n(<code>self.cfg.cure_pass_ceiling</code>) instead of the module-level<br />\n<code>CURE_PASS_CEILING</code> literal they read before this task.</p>\n<pre><code>The quantity bounded is the RUN-wide total across every approach and\nboth cure channels (`LoopSupervisor._cure_passes_for_run`: review's\n`curePasses` plus the gate's `gateCurePasses`), which is what makes the\nrequirement's claim -- &quot;a run cannot loop cure -&gt; reject -&gt; cure\nindefinitely&quot; -- actually true. A per-approach cap cannot: every replan\nstarts an approach whose own counter reads `0`, so the cycle would run\non for as many approaches as the run has budget for.\n\nConfigured to **2** here, below the module default of 3, and driven as a\nrepeated reject-then-cure sequence: review spends pass 1, the peer gate\nspends pass 2 out of the SAME run budget, and every rejection after\nthat -- including the FIRST rejection over a freshly replanned approach,\nwhich a per-approach cap would have granted -- is refused by the ceiling\nalone, with all blocking findings still `curable: true` throughout (no\nincurable finding, no criteria-tamper finding, no superset repeat is\ndoing the stopping). The refusals fall through to the ordinary\nreplan-then-finish edges and the run reaches `failed`, a\n`state.TERMINAL_STATES` member, instead of curing forever.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791925216356,"stop":1791925216356,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791925216356,"stop":1791925216357,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791925594462,"stop":1791925594462,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791925594462,"stop":1791925594477,"duration":15},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791925594478,"stop":1791925594488,"duration":10},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791925594478,"stop":1791925594478,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_undo_instant_sleep_patches","time":{"start":1791925594489,"stop":1791925594489,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path","time":{"start":1791925594489,"stop":1791925594